# OpenLineage Metadata Architecture for Databases

This architecture explains how to get metadata from databases (e.g., Postgres) or other storage systems, emit OpenLineage events, and visualize lineage and metadata.

---

## 1) Big Picture (layers)

[Producers / Collectors]
  • Airflow / Spark / dbt (pipeline-aware)
  • DB Crawler (reads system catalogs: Postgres, Snowflake, etc.)
      ↓  (OpenLineage events: Run, Job, Dataset + facets)

[Transport]
  • HTTP → OL endpoint (e.g., Marquez)
  • or Kafka topic (fan-out to multiple consumers)
      ↓

[Storage / Lineage Service]
  • Marquez (OpenLineage reference backend + API)
      ↓

[Consumers / UX]
  • Marquez UI (lineage graph & metadata views)
  • Data Catalog / Governance (optional)
  • Observability / Analytics (optional)

---

## 2) Two complementary ways to **collect** metadata

### A) Pipeline-driven lineage (best fidelity)
- Tools like Airflow / Spark / dbt emit lineage events at run-time.
- Events include inputs, outputs, run state, schema, and owners.
- Flow:
  Airflow task / dbt model / Spark job
        └─ emits OpenLineage event (HTTP/Kafka)
                └─ Marquez stores & serves lineage
                        └─ Marquez UI visualizes DAG/graph

### B) Database-scan lineage (crawler-based)
- For systems without pipeline hooks, use a crawler that queries `information_schema` / catalogs.
- Extracts datasets, relationships, dependencies (views, FKs, procs).
- Emits synthetic Job/Run events into OpenLineage.

Flow:
  Crawler (scheduled)
        └─ reads DB catalogs + parses SQL
              └─ emits OpenLineage events
                    └─ Marquez + UI

---

## 3) Concrete **Postgres** mapping (example)

**Entities:**
- Dataset → `postgres://<cluster>/<db>.<schema>.<table>`
- Job → logical transform (Airflow task ID, dbt model, or crawler synthetic job)
- Run → single execution (UUID, timestamps, state)

**Examples:**

### (i) Airflow → Postgres
Airflow task (extract_users)
   reads: postgres://prod/app.public.users
   writes: postgres://prod/dwh.stage.users_stg
   ↓ emits OL event (HTTP)
Marquez stores & UI shows lineage edge.

### (ii) dbt → Postgres
dbt model (dim_customers)
   sources: users, invoices
   target: dwh.marts.dim_customers
   ↓ emits OL event
Marquez UI shows graph of sources → model.

### (iii) DB crawler
Crawler scans Postgres, parses views & FKs, emits events nightly.

